dit card or another payment method accepted by Max It: bank card, Google Pay, Apple Pay, and Samsung Pay. Do I need to log in to my account every time I want to top up? Yes, you need to log in to your account to send top-ups. From your customer area, you can view your purchase history and easily make another purchase. What is an FCFA top-up? An FCFA top-up is a credit expressed in West African CFA francs (FCFA) for Orange, Telecel, and Moov Africa customers. It credits the recipient’s main balance with this amount. The recipient will use the credit according to their pricing plan. What is the best internet top-up in Mali ? For one-time use, a 100 MB/day pass should be enough. For longer browsing, choose weekly or monthly data packs (starting from 1 GB). How can I top up an Orange number from another country? Just enter your recipient's phone number and our system will display the top-up catalog of the operator. Depending on the operator, several types of top-ups may be available: - CREDIT: to top up an amount in local currency to the main balance - PACK: to top up voice minutes, SMS, and data - INTERNET: to top up only data Choose the top-up that suits your needs best to send it to your recipient's phone. Then log in to your customer account or create one. Finally, confirm your purchase and pay with your bank card. The credit is instantly sent to the recipient's phone. How can I buy an Orange bundle in Mali? Select “Orange”, enter the recipient’s number, choose the amount in euros or FCFA and pay: the credit appears on the recipient’s line within seconds. Our system displays the operator’s catalog once you type in the number. You can choose between: - CREDIT - PACK (voice, SMS, data) - INTERNET (data only) Log in or create an account and pay securely. The credit is sent instantly. How can I top up an Telecel number from another country? I"}, {"url": "https://maxit.orange.com/fr/page-pays-mali.html", "retrieval_score": 0.44999999999999996, "title": "", "content": "ha