line and in-store. A woman sitting on a couch, holding her phone and a credit card, appears focused on making a purchase. Card-linked installments Mastercard Installments Payment Services enables issuers to add installments as a feature on their existing card portfolios. Consumers can choose to pay in installments using their existing card, both during purchase and post purchase. Get started Check out our developer documentation and experience design guides. Mastercard Installments for developers Detailed information on implementation, experience design, use cases and more. Learn more opens in a new tab Experience design guide It’s easier than ever to develop Mastercard Installments in your own digital environment. Explore opens in a new tab Contact us Get in touch with your Mastercard representative to learn more. Contact us Mastercard logo. [1] Mastercard: World Payments Advisory, 2023. [2] PYMNTS & Sezzle study, BNPL Used as Budgeting Tool, Especially by Millennialls, Says Sezzle CEO, 2023. opens in a new tab [3] FYMNTS.com. Report: 70% of BNPL Users Would Use Book Instaliment Ontions. If Available opens in a new tab , 2022. [4] Harvard Business Review, Research: How 'Buy Now, Pay Later' Is Changing Consumer Spending opens in a new tab , 2024 Home Payments Consumer payments Consumer Solutions - Next Generation Payments We're always here when you need us Need help? Get support Report a lost or stolen card Find ATM FAQs COMPANY About Careers opens in a new tab Newsroom Investor Relations opens in a new tab Global Locations LEGAL & PRIVACY Privacy & Data Responsibility Binding Corporate Rules (BCRs) MASTERCARD SITES Priceless.com opens in a new tab Mastercard Services opens in a new tab Mastercard Developers opens in a new tab Mastercard Marketing Center opens in a new tab Center for Inclusive Growth opens in a new tab © 1994-2026 Mastercard. Privacy Terms Manage cookies Select a country Afghanistan (English) A"}, {"url": "https://www.mastercard.com/fr/fr/business/p